        headline: "Preserve Mercurial identity, history, and publication distinctions",
        boundary: "Model Mercurial from its own authorities in extdeps: portable changeset identity versus clone-local revision, file revisions and manifests, parents/heads, bookmarks, named and topological branches, tags, phases, repository availability, subrepositories, and optional evolution metadata. No Git vocabulary or common adapter appears.",
        displaced_cost: "Prevents bookmark from becoming ref, named branch from becoming pointer, local revision from becoming portable identity, or phase from becoming one visibility bit.",
        first_slice: "Land cited Mercurial types and one bounded state/change fixture that captures, projects, and independently reads back while leaving ungrounded write capability unavailable.",
        red_control: "Clone-local revision may change while changeset identity does not; public/draft/secret remain distinct; bookmark, named branch, and head cannot collapse; absent transaction evidence stays unavailable.",
